# Real survey data — never committed.
# DZT headers can carry GPS, and DZG files certainly do. Publishing
# archaeological site locations is not reversible. Committed fixtures must be
# synthetic, or truncated and coordinate-scrubbed after inspection.
packages/nsgeo-core/tests/data/local/*
!packages/nsgeo-core/tests/data/local/README.md

# Belt and braces: survey data is ignored by EXTENSION anywhere in the tree,
# not just inside the drop directory. A stray file in the repo root or copied
# into fixtures/ would otherwise be committed silently.
#
# Committing a scrubbed fixture is therefore a deliberate act requiring
# `git add -f`. That is intentional.
#
# GSSI
*.[dD][zZ][tT]
*.[dD][zZ][gG]
*.[dD][zZ][xX]
# MALA
*.[rR][dD]3
*.[rR][dD]7
*.[rR][aA][dD]
*.[cC][oO][rR]
# Sensors & Software
*.[dD][tT]1

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# QGIS
*.qgs~
*.qgz~

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
